	"display_name": "Fort Aldmere's gate garrison",
	"description": "P36 (plan M6-M9 §5.4, §5.7, §5.10, §2.12): the garrison before Fort Aldmere's gate - a pike formation of ten and its banner before the gate (stage >= 4), in front of the west bastion beside the road's approach, four wall archers on the gate bastions (elevation markers: their posts) and the crews of the bastions' two ballistae (faction aldmere: neutral until offended - breaching the gate is an offence, so the breach path fights them). While the giant has the herald's leave to parley, or carries Brannock's banner within 150 m of the gate, and the gate stands, the garrison stands down (stand_down_when): the parley path walks up to the gate unharmed whatever Aldmere's standing. Leash 60 m. M9 gate: the pikes' post moved from the gate's line (pivot (650, -79.1)) to (626, -75): every titan path into the bailey crosses the broken or opened gate on its link from (650, -87) to (650, -105), and the formation stood on that line 5-9 m before it, a wall of bodies no stage 4-6 giant could pass with the garrison alive (the M9 confirmation's gateway stucks); tests/gate/test_fort_gateway.gd. M9 gate (lane ironreg): once the gate is breached the garrison falls back to its posts and stands down - until the giant enters the bailey (this visit: a load starts a new one) or the battle is settled (boss.corvane.outcome), unless he strikes one of its members (its provoked flag) - so the fort gate's waystone, 25-35 m from its pikes and archers, is no fight to respawn into: a death in the bailey reloads the breach's checkpoint (the gate broken) and the giant walks back in. Before, the breach roused it for good and after each reload it held the giant at the waystone (aldmere_e5_ir5: twice for 130 s, until he died); in the bailey it is the battle's (stood out; its two wall crews serve the bastions' ballistae, held until the Charge). M9 gate (final): its provoked flag counts since the current stand-down began, and the gate's fall begins a new one (EncounterDirector._p29_on_object_destroyed): a blow on a member standing down for the banner or the parley before the breach no longer keeps it roused after it; a blow after the breach provokes it as before.",
